src/rocqdep_lexer.mll is tools/coqdep/lib/lexer.mll of the Rocq Prover 9.2.0,
copied unchanged. It is the lexer `rocq dep` uses to find the Require
statements of a .v file. Its authors (INRIA, CNRS and contributors) distribute
it under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1, and it keeps that
license here; the original notice is in the file's header. Refresh the copy
from the Rocq sources of the switch when the Rocq version changes.

It is copied rather than linked because rocq-runtime.coqdeplib cannot be
linked into this program: that library's Args module registers the warning
name "unknown-option", which Rocq's own library/goptions.ml registers too, and
the second registration aborts the process at startup.

The program also links the Rocq runtime libraries (rocq-runtime and the
libraries it installs, LGPL 2.1) at build time, which the LGPL permits: the
sources of this program are available, so the library part stays replaceable.
